# Self-hosted production build (a private/personal deployment behind a live
# api/, e.g. a self-managed VPS) -- distinct from .env.production, which the
# public GitHub Pages build always uses and which stays "static" per AD-57
# (docs/ARCHITECTURE_DECISIONS.md: no live backend on the *public* site,
# ever). AD-57 explicitly keeps a live api/ available as a permanent
# local-only/self-hosted option; this file is that option's production-build
# variant. Build with: npm run build -w web -- --mode selfhosted
#
# Requires a live api/ reachable at the same origin under /api (see
# deploy/nginx/egx-genom.conf), with DECISION_DATA_DIR set to a real
# `agx run` --data-dir for Decision Center / Capital Allocation to work --
# see README.md's "Personalized decisions" section.
VITE_DATA_PROVIDER=api
